     "evaporation",
     "condensation",
     "melting"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Evaporation is water turning into vapour at any temperature, faster when it is warm and windy. Condensation is vapour turning back into drops on a cold surface, like drops on a cold glass.\nMelting is ice turning into water, and freezing is water turning into ice. Heat is taken in for melting and given out for freezing.\nBoiling is rapid evaporation at 100 degrees Celsius."
    }
